  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Ether",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 15,
    "summary": "Millions of the Jaredites are slain in battle—Shiz and Coriantumr assemble all the people to mortal combat—The Spirit of the Lord ceases to strive with them—The Jaredite nation is utterly destroyed—Only Coriantumr remains.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass when Coriantumr had recovered of his wounds, he began to remember the words which Ether had spoken unto him.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 90,
            "end": 95,
            "text": "Ether 13:20 (20–21)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ether 15:1",
        "book": "Ether",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "He saw that there had been slain by the sword already nearly two millions of his people, and he began to sorrow in his heart; yea, there had been slain two millions of mighty men, and also their wives and their children.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 61,
            "end": 73,
            "text": "Ether 1:43."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Ether 1:43.",
            "prettyString": "Ether 1:43",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "ether",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 1,
                    "end": 1,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 43,
                        "end": 43
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ether 15:2",
        "book": "Ether",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "He began to repent of the evil which he had done; he began to remember the words which had been spoken by the mouth of all the prophets, and he saw them that they were fulfilled thus far, every whit; and his soul mourned and refused to be comforted.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 213,
            "end": 220,
            "text": "TG Mourning."
          },
          {
            "start": 239,
            "end": 248,
            "text": "Gen. 37:35; Moses 7:44. TG Comfort."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Mourning.",
            "prettyString": "TG Mourning",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Mourning",
                "entryId": "tg-mourning",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ether 15:3",
        "book": "Ether",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that he wrote an epistle unto Shiz, desiring him that he would spare the people, and he would give up the kingdom for the sake of the lives of the people.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ether 15:4",
        "book": "Ether",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that when Shiz had received his epistle he wrote an epistle unto Coriantumr, that if he would give himself up, that he might slay him with his own sword, that he would spare the lives of the people.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ether 15:5",
        "book": "Ether",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that the people repented not of their iniquity; and the people of Coriantumr were stirred up to anger against the people of Shiz; and the people of Shiz were stirred up to anger against the people of Coriantumr; wherefore, the people of Shiz did give battle unto the people of Coriantumr.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ether 15:6",
        "book": "Ether",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "And when Coriantumr saw that he was about to fall he fled again before the people of Shiz.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ether 15:7",
        "book": "Ether",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that he came to the waters of Ripliancum, which, by interpretation, is large, or to exceed all; wherefore, when they came to these waters they pitched their tents; and Shiz also pitched his tents near unto them; and therefore on the morrow they did come to battle.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ether 15:8",
        "book": "Ether",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that they fought an exceedingly sore battle, in which Coriantumr was wounded again, and he fainted with the loss of blood.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ether 15:9",
        "book": "Ether",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that the armies of Coriantumr did press upon the armies of Shiz that they beat them, that they caused them to flee before them; and they did flee southward, and did pitch their tents in a place which was called Ogath.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ether 15:10",
        "book": "Ether",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that the army of Coriantumr did pitch their tents by the hill Ramah; and it was that same hill where my father Mormon did hide up the records unto the Lord, which were sacred.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 142,
            "end": 146,
            "text": "Morm. 6:6."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Morm. 6:6.",
            "prettyString": "Mormon 6:6",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "mormon",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 6,
                    "end": 6,
                    "verses": [
