        "book": "Ether",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that when it was night they were weary, and retired to their camps; and after they had retired to their camps they took up a howling and a lamentation for the loss of the slain of their people; and so great were their cries, their howlings and lamentations, that they did rend the air exceedingly.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 159,
            "end": 170,
            "text": "TG Mourning."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Mourning.",
            "prettyString": "TG Mourning",
            "references": [
              {
