        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ether 15:16",
        "book": "Ether",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that on the morrow they did go again to battle, and great and terrible was that day; nevertheless, they conquered not, and when the night came again they did rend the air with their cries, and their howlings, and their mournings, for the loss of the slain of their people.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ether 15:17",
        "book": "Ether",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that Coriantumr wrote again an epistle unto Shiz, desiring that he would not come again to battle, but that he would take the kingdom, and spare the lives of the people.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ether 15:18",
        "book": "Ether",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "But behold, the Spirit of the Lord had ceased striving with them, and Satan had full power over the hearts of the people; for they were given up unto the hardness of their hearts, and the blindness of their minds that they might be destroyed; wherefore they went again to battle.",
        "footNotes": [
